highlight.js (custom build)
Version: 11.11.1
Licence: BSD-3-Clause
Source:  https://www.npmjs.com/package/highlight.js (LICENSE from the highlight.js@11.11.1 package)

This file (highlight.min.js) is NOT the upstream distributable — it is a
custom bundle built from highlight.js's own source: `highlight.js/lib/core`
plus the `bash`, `c`, `go`, `json`, `python` and `shell` grammars and the
`plaintext` fallback — exactly the languages the shipped docs and the landing
fence, and nothing else. It is produced locally with esbuild and vendored here
so the site never fetches highlighting from a CDN.

`c` and `python` were added when docs/c-abi.md and docs/quickstart.md started
fencing them; before that they fell through to plaintext and rendered as flat
grey, which looks like a palette problem and is actually a missing grammar.
`scripts/check-docs-chrome.mjs` now loads this bundle and fails if any fence
in the corpus names a language it does not carry, so the next one cannot ship
unnoticed.

Rebuild it by installing highlight.js@11.11.1 and esbuild, and running esbuild
against an entry file that imports core plus the languages listed above:

    esbuild entry.mjs --bundle --minify --format=iife --outfile=highlight.min.js

registering each with `hljs.registerLanguage(name, grammar)` and exposing the
result as `window.hljs`. Aliases (`sh`, `golang`, `text`, `py`, `h`, `jsonc`)
come from the grammars themselves and need no separate registration.

